# Feature workflow

Use this for any non-trivial feature. For epics, one feature = one branch = one PR (parallel features use separate git worktrees).

## 1. Plan

- Switch to **Plan mode** (Cursor) or ask Claude to plan only without editing (CLI: be explicit in the prompt).
- Produce a short written plan; wait for human approval before coding.

## 2. Implement (local)

- One feature per worktree when working in parallel:
  `git worktree add ../<repo>-wt/<feature-slug> main && cd ../<repo>-wt/<feature-slug>`
- Match existing code style. Run before opening a PR:
  - `npm run lint` (or project equivalent)
  - `npm run test:unit` (required)
  - `npm run test:e2e` (best-effort unless the feature is UI-critical — then required before PR; see gates below)

## 3. Open PR

- Title: Conventional Commits format (`feat(scope): subject`).
- Trivial PRs (docs-only, version bump, typo): add label `no-claude-loop`.
- UI / UX / flows that need human eyes: add label `awaiting-e2e`.
- Want to review yourself before the bot keeps fixing: add label `human-gate`.
- Example:
  `gh pr create --title "feat(scope): …" --body "…" --label awaiting-e2e`

## 4. CI review loop (automatic)

- Push triggers Claude review + up to 3 fix iterations (subscription-billed).
- Labels pause automation:
  - `human-gate` — no auto-fix rounds; you review manually. Remove label to resume.
  - `awaiting-e2e` — on CI pass, bot waits for you to run e2e and remove the label.
- Watch the PR on GitHub (notifications) or Actions tab.

## 5. Finalize

- After CI loop passes (and e2e gate cleared if applicable), run **`/babysit`** (skill) to chase merge-ready state: comments, CI, conflicts.
- Merge when green and you are satisfied.

## Headless (no IDE)

- Open a GitHub Issue per feature; comment `@claude implement per issue description`.
- Same CI loop applies to the resulting PR. Use labels on the PR as above.

## Parallel features

- Never implement two features in the same worktree.
- If two features touch the same files, sequence them — do not rely on parallel PRs.
